 ## Background
-The concept of adaptive density control was introduced in the original 3D Gaussian Splatting paper by Kerbl et al. (2023) [S1, unofficial]. The method was designed to handle the trade-off between reconstruction fidelity and computational efficiency by dynamically adjusting the number of primitives. Since then, numerous variants have been proposed to address specific issues such as uncontrolled growth [S1, unofficial], blurry backgrounds [S1, unofficial], and unpredictable model size [S3].
